As far as RMS record marks, you might want to investigate the use
of UCX> ADD EXPORT/OPTION=DATA_CONVERSION to allow the NFS server
to convert typical VMS variable record files to a stream format that
UNIX can handle more easily.  This is supposed to be the default.
Should allow you to read postscript files as text.  Anyway, read the
help on this option to see if it's what you want.

>  Now I installed posix on our alpha cluster, and I tried to export
>the posix file systems to Ultrix.  One the DECstation, I mounted the
>VMS disks fine, but I was supprised so find out that they belong to
>"nobody" instead of root. It did not bother me until I logged in  as
>an ordinary user and tried  to read files. It always gives me 
>"vmsdkb0: Not owner".  If I log in as root, I can read the files
>without any problem, and see all those files has mode 755. What is
>wrong with those posix files?

What does

UCX> SHOW PROXY
show you?  This is the thing that maps UNIX user IDs to VMS user ids.
If UCX can't find a useful mapping, it usually reports "nobody".



