The DECUS '94/Anaheim Seminars and Symposium national event is being held
December 10-15, 1994.  The deadline for submitting seminar and session
abstracts was originally June 3rd.  Seminar submissions are still due June 3.
However, the session submission deadline has been extended to June 10.
 
The focus of DECUS '94/Anaheim remains on creating and managing systems
that are increasingly distributed, multiplatform, and multivendor.
Submissions of seminars and sessions are invited in several major tracks
and on supporting technologies.  These tracks are described in detail in the
CFP for the Anaheim event.  Supporting technologies include, but are
not necessarily limited to, OpenVMS, Alpha AXP RISC architecture, storage,
and peripherals.

The DECUS '94/Anaheim Program Committee is interested in user-submitted
talks on a number of topics related to OpenVMS, AXP RISC, storage and
peripherals.  (Note that these topics are just a subset of those that
will be presented in Anaheim; for a complete list of topics, please
consult the full Call for Participation (CFP) form.)

In particular, we are looking for user-provided sessions on

  OpenVMS DCL programming and lexical functions
  OpenVMS DCL for UNIX Users
  OpenVMS logical names (novice, intermediate (use in system mgmt))
  OpenVMS batch/print configuration and maintenance (novice)
  OpenVMS backup strategies and solutions (user experience)
  OpenVMS account management strategies and solutions (user experience)
  OpenVMS accounting strategies and solutions (user experience)
  OpenVMS system tuning (novice, intermediate, advanced, using
	SYSGEN, AUTOGEN parameters)
  OpenVMS using new V6 system services (intermediate)
  OpenVMS writing a device driver (user experience)
  OpenVMS System Management for UNIX System Administrators
  OpenVMS SDA: Tips and Techniques of Use
  Developing robust systems using DCE (user experience)
  Postscript (novice, advanced)
  Terminal server configuration (user experience)
  Network Printer in a Heterogeneous Network Environment strategies and
	solutions (user experience)

We would also like to put together some user panels:

  OpenVMS mixed-architecture (VAX,AXP) VMScluster migration experiences
  OpenVMS V6.1 upgrade experiences
  Migration to Storageworks (user experiences)
  RAID (user experiences)

If you feel that you have something to share in any of these areas, or
in some other related area that we haven't mentioned, please submit a
session for Anaheim.  Sessions are normally 30 or 60 minutes in length. 
If you are interested in presenting a one- or two-day seminar on an issue
related to OpenVMS, Alpha AXP RISC architecture, storage, or
peripherals, or if you'd like to participate with other users in a
panel, please contact Kevin Hansher at 614-424-4008 or hansher@decus.org.

To submit a session or seminar, you should obtain and fill out a CFP form.
You can obtain a CFP form via anonymous ftp to decus.org in file
[.decus94-anaheim]cfp.txt, via Gopher or WWW to URL gopher://Gopher.
DECUS.Org.:70/00gopher_root1:[decus94-anaheim]cfp.txt, or via e-mail
by sending a one-line message GET [DECUS94-ANAHEIM]CFP.TXT to
address mailserv@decus.org.

All seminar submissions must be received in the DECUS office by 11:00pm PDT,
Friday, June 3, 1994.  All session submissions must be received in the DECUS
office by 11:00pm PDT, Friday, June 10, 1994. Please submit ONE seminar or
symposium session per form.  Forms may be photocopied for additional
submissions.  Send Your Submission(s) to the DECUS office via postal mail to
DECUS - Submission Processing, SHR3-1/T25 334 South Street, Shrewsbury, MA
01545-4195; via FAX to 508-841-3357; or via e-mail to submissions@decus.org.
General questions regarding submissions may be directed to Gloria Caputo at
508-841-3530.
