Good luck converting the DB15 to serial!  Last time I checked, it is only
capable of passing keyboard and mouse inputs to the appropriate kernel drivers.
There is no way to pass standard output (characters) to this port.  You will
need to use the DB25 connector.  I had to go through this nonsense about 2
years ago when my outfit received 2 DECSystem 5000-240's.  What's the
difference between a DECSystem and a DECStation? The video adapter (or lack
thereof).  So this $25,000 box shows up and the bozo's at the integration
house didn't even bother to check to see if you could run a console from the
serial port.  Turns out there is a way to do it, by setting a monitor variable
called console to the "correct" value.  On the back of the 5000-240 the ports
are numbered 2 and 3.  We chose 3.  The video adapter has a value of either 0
or *, I can't remember which.  You might also check for a switch.  We just
converted a VAXStation 4000-60 to a VAXSystem 4000-60 (yeah, I know, no such
beast in the DEC catalog).  Anyway, there was a dip switch on the front of the
machine that had some sort of icon on it.  The console variable trick didn't
work on the VAXStation, so in desperation I tried this dip switch. Worked like
a charm.  So, I'd suspect that yeah, toggle it to think that it's a MicroVAX.


