There have been various posts about how disappointingly slow the serial ports
are on a variety of workstations (DEC in particular).  A number of people
then suggest that even PCs can do much better.  Of course, this is untrue.
Admittedly on a PC doing very little you can wind the serial ports up to their
rated speeds, but once you start doing interesting things it all goes horribly
wrong.
We have a 3100-40 running Pathworks to 150 clients.  Of course its overloaded
but I'm certain that everything will continue to work (including those slow
serial ports).  Now I don't think that you get the same robustness under
overload out of your average PC, especially if you are still foolish enough to
use an ISA bus machine.

