Now, I must admit that I don't run 150 pathworks clients, but I
do run fairly heavy loads on a 486DX33 under SunSoft Interactive
Unix.  Load factors of 4 are not uncommon.  The system is equipped
with a 2-port and two 4-port dumb serial cards that use
NS-16550AFN UARTS.  Yes, it is ISA bus with only an ESDI disk
drive.  It is certainly the poor step child in our environment,
running news, fax services, and a few other applications that we
can't run elsewhere.

Under these loads, multiple modems with DTE rates of 115kbps
working UUCP and PPP connections operate with an insignificant
number of errors (less than 10 per month) according to the PPP
and UUCP logs.

