complete failure to support dialup networking capabilities that
have been around for years by saying that PC systems can't do it.
PC systems really can't do lots of things.  No argument.  But PCs
can easily support this kind of async load.  Workstation vendors
supply garbage async hardware and software.  A PC running Unix
with a $30 serial card _can_ do much, much better.
