As another reply pointed out, NetWorker uses its own tape format. It's
especially designed for easy recovery, and to allow multiple clients
to interleave data on the same tape for speedier backups.

POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore is Digital's version of Legato
Corporation's NetWorker software, which is available on many UNIX
platforms, and also on Netware servers.  The tapes are interchangeable
among all the NetWorker implementations.

I have a lot of experience with NetWorker, mostly positive :-)


