>
>I have just acquired a 19" DEC color monitor that I would like to use with
>my VGA card (ATI VGAWONDER GT).  The monitor has only RGB inputs (i.e. no
>sync).  I assume it syncs to green. So, should i merely need to connect the
>corresponding colors from the VGA card up to the monitor's BNC connectors?
>Will that work or do I need to do something else.

I looked for this info myself a while back.  I found an answer in
comp.sys.apollo FAQ.  I'll attach the postscript file that shows the 
schematic.

The problem with this arrangement is that the DEC monitor is not a
multisync type display so it cannot sync on the regular VGA frequency.
However, it can do high resolution modes.  So make sure your autoexec.bat 
starts windows because you won't be able to see anything till it goes
into hires mode.

--Eric

