In article <Cq7u4C.Aq@news.ci.ua.pt>, cooker@ci.ua.pt (Fernando Cozinheiro) writes:
>
>I want to install an HP tape driver  DAT-DDS on my  DECstation  5000/25,
>using  SCSI  interface...  but I don't know how to solve the  associated
>problems:
>
>	1. I have no /dev/rmt* devices;
>	2. I don't know how to make the device file;

The first is solved by the 2nd; /dev/MAKEDEV.

When the system boots look at the boot messages to determine
the "tz" device for the drive.  It may look something like:

tz5 at asc0 slave 5 (TZxx) [ DEC     TZ85     (C) DEC 2708 ]

The name of interest is "tz5".  Then use MAKEDEV to create
the special device files:

# cd /dev
# MAKEDEV tz5

If special files for another tape drive already exist, it will
use the next logical tape number; mt0, mt1, mt2, etc.

