I hope this doesn't fan the flames, but I couldn't resist.  Digital has
problems, but so does much of the industry.  Over the next several years
the entire industry will continuing moving to lower and lower margins.

While the red ink has not gone away, there are several bright spots for Digital.
Digital's disk and PC businesses are doing very well.  According to one report I
read recently, Digital is a 10 ten PC vendor (7th is the actual guess).  The
software services business for DEC isn't doing to bad either.  Digital still
has cash and unlike most companies has very little long term debt.  The
new Alpha 2100 boxes look like winners and the LinkWorks workflow/groupware
product looks good.  As usual, Digital continues to have the technology but
not the sales/marketing/etc to get to the customers.

While Digital may be a VERY different company in 5 or 10 years, my bet is
that they will still exist.

