I've used the following printcap with a wide variety of PostScript printers
(including several models of the Apple LaserWriter), with great success.  
You may need to change /dev/tty00 if you have more than one serial port.   
You might also want to change all of the instances of "lp1" to "lp2" (or 3,
or 4, etc) if you have more than one printer.

After installing the new printcap, you'll want to run (as root):
	/etc/lpc abort all
	/etc/lpc clean all
	/etc/lpc restart all

to get the print queue back in order, before you try to print anything.


lp|lp1|PostScript Laser:\
	:af=/usr/adm/lp1acct:\
	:br#9600:\
	:ct=dev:\
	:fc#0177777:\
	:fs#03:\
	:if=/usr/lib/lpdfilters/ln03rof:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lp1err:\
	:lp=/dev/tty00:\
	:mc#20:\
	:mx#0:\
	:of=/usr/lib/lpdfilters/ln03rof:\
	:pl#66:\
	:pw#80:\
	:rw:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd1:\
	:sh:\
	:uv=4.0:\
	:xc#0177777:\
	:xf=/usr/lib/lpdfilters/xf:\
	:xs#044000:


