Do you mean DEMPR?  If so, the answer is NO.  The DEMPR is a repeater, and
all repeaters operate at wire speed.  If your network and its components
conform to the relevant standards, it will work at any load.

Some packet switching devices (bridges, routers, etc) have performance
limitations, but repeaters never do, by definition.

