sturges@brahma-client.cs.odu.edu (Jonathan Sturges) writes:

>Kenneth Moyers 21123 (kenwm@nyquist..bellcore.com) wrote:
>: RD54 taken from an external drive box, but the Mvax dosn't seem to
>: recognize it.  Can someone tell me what the jumper settings on the RD54
>: should be?  Any other advice on getting the RD54 going in place of the 
>: RD53 would be appreciated.

>I, too, just pulled an RD54 (actually, a plain-jane XT2190) from an old
>PC, but can't get my MicroVAX to format the damn thing.  It does format in
>a PC.

There are two styles of RD54 - one in which the jumpers are marked

	123456

and one in which they are marked

	1c23c4

If you have the former, the ds3 jumper (the default, and what works on
a uVax) should be 2-3.  If the latter, 3-c.

					Megan Gentry
					Former RT-11 Developer



