Here's one reason to update your DECServer 200 software, from the release
notes for the V3.3 version:

     "1.3.2  "SET PORT" Crash Code 200 -

      1.3.2.1  How To Identify The Problem -

      Server Crashes with code 200 when  a  non-priviledged  user  tries  to
      perform  a  "SET PORT <n><c>".  Where <n> is any valid port number and
      <c> is any alphanumeric character.

      1.3.2.2  How To Work Around The Problem -

      Install BL37C image or later immediately."

We have our dial-in lines set so that an initial password is required before
the user calling in even gets the server's prompt; the "security" keeps the
user from using the "show" command to see what nodes and services are 
available.

Hope this helps,

