In article <1994May16.160652.25501@sol.UVic.CA>, zapantis@uvphys.phys.uvic.ca
(Nik Zapantis) writes:
>A month or two ago, I read somewhere (maybe the Digital Customer Update) that
>the latest version of the DECPrint Supervisor (DCPS) had support for the
>Tektronix Phaser colour PS printer (I've tried to locate the article, but 
>have not been able to find it).
>
>I've looked at the SPD for DCPS in the latest CD (v 1.0B) but the Tek Phaser
>printer is not listed (even though the Tek 220 is the same as DEC's LF02).
>
>Does anyone know if the Tek phaser 200/220 printers are supported?
>Maybe someone from DEC could provide some information?

DEC's predecessor software (CPS) was made to specifically *not* work with
non-DEC priners.  The current software (DCPS) was made to work with non-DEC
printers as much as possible, provided that the 'foreign' PAK (DCPS-Open) was
present on the system.  [Also, the CPS per-printer license was changed to
per-CPU for DCPS.]  Generally, all postscript printers obeying standard Adobe
postscript level 1 and level 2 code work properly with DCPS.  In the case of
multiple-personality printers, you sometimes have to disable the "other"
non-postscript language, but it otherwise works fine.

I've used DCPS with the Tektronix Phaser 200e and other printers and it works
fine.

I don't think you'll see anything from DEC saying that any specific non-DEC
printers are fully supported though...
