Malcolm MacArthur writes:

>We've acquired a DEC Rainbow 100+ with full-height hard disk, twin floppy 
>drive, etc. (At auction for a ridiculously low price :-)

>However, when powered up, the hard drive spins itself up but nothing else 
>happens. Diagnostic lights 1,2 & 3 are on. What do the lights mean?
>We'd read the FM, but we didn't get one.

The message means "main board interrupts off."  The "corrective action" 
is as follows (from one of the diagnostic manuals):

"If this error occurs during power-up or self-test, turn power off, then 
on again.  If error persists, replace system module; if this error occurs 
during an application program, the error can be a program bug (in either 
the operating system or the application program) that turns off the 
interrupts for an excessive time."

    -- Carl Neiburger ( carln@netcom.com ) 


