As far as basic PostScript compatibility goes, the PrintServer 20 uses
a standard Adobe PostScript interpreter - all of the core operators are
there and if I may say so, they work fine.  The number one problem that
you are likely to run into is that the PrintServers did not have the
"LaserWriter Compatibility" operators such as the userdict pagesize
operators.  These ops are not core PostScript and are not included in
all but the most recent versions of the PrintServer software.
(The PrintServer line is as old as the original LaserWriter - not sure
which is older - but there was not an issue of being compatibile with
an LW when the PrintServer's started.)  If the errors you are getting
are due to these ops, you an try defining them yourself as noops...
(An example of a compat op would be "letter" or "a4".)

Anyway, I'll forward your message along to a couple other people here
and see what they say.

