Sorry Wayne, we don't have cross-compilers from Alpha to VAX,
and there are none planned that I know of.  There are technical
reasons why this would be problematical to provide even if there
were a large demand for it [non-productized cross compilers from
VAX to Alpha were developed for the port, but not crossed in the
other direction].

In a previous life, I was very pleased when Sun came out with
cross compilers in both directions when they first introduced the
SPARC; and I was *extremely* displeased when support for them was
dropped by the time our company was ready to start using them.
Cross compilers introduce a substantial additional support burden
over the long term, but the need for them does diminish as a new
architecture gains acceptance.  Rather than do a now-you-have-it
now-you-don't, the product compilers were native-only from day 1.

