You don't say what OS you will be using, but if it is OSF/1, my advice is to
go with the RRD-43 and forget trying to make a third party drive work.  I have
been unable to get an NEC drive to mount any type of CD under OSF/1.  The basic
problem is that OSF/1 expects 512 byte blocks whereas the typical CD-ROM drive
defaults to 2048.  My attempts to compensate via making a custom entry in the
/sys/data/cam_data.c file have been to no avail, and inquiries on the net have
yielded no advice.  If someone out there has been successful at running a 3rd
party CD-ROM drive under OSF/1, I would very much like to hear about it.

