Wel, I will reply with a more general "how to make a noop" since this can
be used for many other things, not just pagesize operators on old versions
of PrintServer software (newer PrintServer printers do have these ops).

Anyway, to make an operator do nothing for just your file, edit it and add
the following to the top of the file (after the first line which should be
%!PS<some version #>...):

/operator_name { } def	% define operator_name to do nothing

For example, if you have a file which uses the letter operator and you want
to print it to a printer which does not have that operator, add the
following line:

/letter { } def

If you want to do it for more than just your job, or don't want to edit
your file, you should make the definition outsde the server loop which
requires knowledge of your printers password.  As an example, let's say
your PrintServer's password was (password), and you wanted to define letter
as a noop persistently across jobs (this does not last across power
cycles), send the file:

%!PS
severdict begin (password) exitserver
/letter { } def


Hope that helps,

