andrew@helena.rdt.monash.edu.au (Andrew Moore) writes:
Andrew> I am having a little trouble with a 3100 running Ultrix 4.3a
Andrew> For various reasons the kernel panics, unfortunatly when it
Andrew> panics the system freezes (does not get to dump a core, etc.)

To force a crash dump on a DECstation 3100, you must first do a

>> setenv bootmode d

at the console monitor to disable the self-test after a reset.  After
a reset, you can jump to the crash dump routine with

>> go 0x80030008

(that address should work with any model DECstation and any version of
Ultrix--I've never figured out why people bother figuring out the
actual address of the crash dump routine when the kernel keeps a jump
to it for you just after the boot entry point).

