From: irv@dizzy.cplex.com (Irv Lustig)
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
Subject: Summary of modem fix for AXP
Date: 6 May 1994 14:37:33 GMT
Organization: CPLEX Optimization, Inc.
Lines: 26
Distribution: world
Message-ID: <2qdknd$j5p@c3po.jvnc.net>
NNTP-Posting-Host: lustig.jvnc.net

I eventually got my modem to work.  Here is what I did:

Create an entry in /etc/uugettydefs with the following:

19200 # B19200 CS8 HUPCL # B19200 SANE HUPCL # login: # 19200

Create an entry in /etc/inittab with the following

30:23:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t 60 tty00 19200

There were 2 keys here:

1) In inittab, you need runlevels at 23 (the man page on uugetty has
   this wrong)
2) For some reason, communication between the AXP and the modem
   would only occur at 19200.  There is a chance that the modem
   may have locked the baud rate to this.

Thanks to Eric Osborne (edo@cso.dec.com) for the inittab hint,
and to the modem gods for helping me find that 19200 was the trick.

