The 'DEC Ada Version 3.1 for DEC OSF/1 AXP Systems' kit
contains 7 subsets, including an Examples subset and a
'DEC Compiled Code Support Library' subset (an RTL used
by several Digital compilers).  If a particular subset's name
is recorded as already installed on the system, the 'setld -l'
command will not offer it for installation again - that is, it
is not shown even though it is on the kit. This can happen if
a subset was installed from the same media previously. or
if a field-test version of that release remains on the system.
Use 'setld -i ' to see what is currently installed, and 'setld -d'
to delete existing subsets, if desired.


