          Reminder and Update: Supercomputing Symposium '94

  This is a reminder that the deadline for SS'94 advance registration was
Friday, May 6. However, because so many registrations are still arriving
via mail and fax, the SS'94 organizing committee has decided to waive the
late registration fee for any registration received by Friday, May 13. This
will allow anyone still undecided about attending the conference to take
another few days to make that decision.

  The summary below is provided to allow prospective attendees determine
whether SS'94 would be of interest to them. If you know anyone you believe
would be interested in SS'94, please forward this message to them.

  The invited speakers are all world class experts in their fields, and
great speakers to boot. They include:
  + Norris Parker Smith [overview of high performance computing]
    * editor-at-large for the "HPCwire Select News" electronic magazine
    * coauthor of the book "The Supercomputer Era"
  + Horst Simon [description of experiences with MPP computing at NAS]
    * department manager with Computer Sciences Corporation
    * supervises research at NASA/Ames NAS facility
  + John Simonds [discussion of digital recording for HDTV and the NII]
    * was Executive Director of the National Storage Industry Consortium
    * spend 39 years with Eastman Kodak's research organization
  + Andrew Bjerring [report on CANARIE]
    * President/CEO, Canadian Network for the Advancement of Research,
      Industry and Education]
    * senior Director of Information Technology Services (Uof Western Ontario)

  Because the number of papers (58 contributed and 10 vendor) is larger
than expected, sessions will be held during the afternoon of Wednesday,
June 8. These sessions will include many interesting presentations as well
as the panel discussion "Vendors' Views of the Future". If at all possible,
you should plan to stay at the conference through Wednesday afternoon.

  The conference social scene includes an early-bird reception, a gourmet
banquet/murder-mystery, and (optionally) a 20% discount on tickets to see
the Toronto production of Miss Saigon - to say nothing of the entire city
of Toronto. See you in Toronto.

  Additional details are available in the CONFERENCE INFORMATION AND
REGISTRATION MATERIALS document. If you do not already have a copy, you can
obtain one using one of the following methods:
  (1) send me your postal address and I will mail it to you.
  (2) download it using anonymous FTP from node "ftp.utirc.utoronto.ca"
      in directory "/pub/SS94". The document is available in two formats:
      PostScript (registration.ps) and ASCII text (registration.txt).
The FTP directory also includes an ASCII list of those papers which have
been accepted for the conference. The file "ss94.papers" contains a list
of the titles and authors sorted alphabetically by title.

  Edmund West (Conference Chair, SS'94)

