If the flow control type is XON and input and output flow control are enabled,
binary file transfers that contain 0x11 and 0x13 values will not transfer
correctly.  The user must either change the flow control type or disable
input and/or output flow control.  A similar flow control configuration change
would typically be required of any modem involved in the configuration.
Use of CTS/RTS flow control avoids this issue.

If SLIP or PPP is used, the terminal server automatically disables XON flow
control while the protocol is active.  But, any modem in the configuration
must be correctly configured.

Hugh

