I would suggest that you try your code on each machine and you
might try an HP735 or IBM RS6000 3XX box. Get a demo of the
machines you're serious about. DEC has been providing an
Alpha machine on the net for test drives. My experience has
been that different codes can behave quite differently on
different machines, in terms of execution time. It depends
on what strengths and weaknesses of each machine a particular
code exercises (cache, memory bandwidth, integer/floating point
ratio, special multiply-add instructions, big performance
hits for divides relative to another machine, etc.). Here's
the DEC instructions (maybe outdated) for using their Alpha box.

