In article <2q67a9$7u1@c3po.jvnc.net>, Irv Lustig <irv@dizzy.uucp> wrote:
>1) We placed the line (see man uugetty)
>
>30:2:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t 60 tty00 9600
>
>in /etc/inittab, typed "init q", and the uugetty process does
>not get started.


Look at the man page again - you missed a field.  The line should
look more like
30:2:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t 60 tty00 9600

I'd actually recommend adding the run level 3, as well, so you end
up with 

30:23:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t 60 tty00 9600

Note that the speed label points to an entry in /etc/gettydefs.  It is
recommended that you use M9600 for a modem.  9600 is really intended for a
direct-connected terminal.  Also, the label at the beginning of the line
usually reflects some indicator of the thing to be spawned, so you might
consider a line like this :

tty00:23:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t 60 tty00 M9600


Hope that helps.

