It looks to me as if the suffix for concurrent use licenses is 3B (for personal
use it is generally 2B).  For example, DEC Fortran for OpenVMS VAX would
be QL-100AA-3B.  I don't have access to the electronic store so I have no
idea if they're shown there.  But they are in the official "price book".

There's no other info you should need - it appears that the suffix is the same
for OpenVMS and DEC OSF/1.  
